# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Background {#background}"
msgstr "Latar belakang {#background}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial shows how to use [SQOA Solver, a Qiskit Function by JIJ](/guides/jij-sqoa-solver), to solve a maximum independent set (MIS) problem with more binary variables than the selected QPU has qubits. The basic steps are to load an MIS instance from the [Quantum Optimization Benchmarking Library (QOBLIB)](https://github.com/ZIB-AOPT/QOBLIB) [\\[1\\]](#references), formulate it in quadratic unconstrained binary optimization (QUBO) form with [qiskit-addon-opt-mapper](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-opt-mapper/), submit it to SQOA Solver for execution on an IBM&reg; QPU, and validate the returned solution.\n"
msgstr "Tutorial ini menunjukkan cara menggunakan [SQOA Solver, sebuah Qiskit Function oleh JIJ](/guides/jij-sqoa-solver), untuk menyelesaikan masalah set tak bersandar maksimum (MIS) dengan lebih banyak pemboleh ubah binari daripada bilangan qubit pada QPU yang dipilih. Langkah asasnya ialah memuatkan satu instans MIS daripada [Quantum Optimization Benchmarking Library (QOBLIB)](https://github.com/ZIB-AOPT/QOBLIB) [\\[1\\]](#references), merumuskannya dalam bentuk pengoptimuman binari tanpa kekangan kuadratik (QUBO) dengan [qiskit-addon-opt-mapper](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-opt-mapper/), menyerahkannya kepada SQOA Solver untuk pelaksanaan pada QPU IBM&reg;, dan mengesahkan penyelesaian yang dikembalikan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The maximum independent set problem {#the-maximum-independent-set-problem}"
msgstr "Masalah set tak bersandar maksimum {#the-maximum-independent-set-problem}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An independent set is a subset of nodes in a graph such that no two selected nodes share an edge. A maximum independent set (MIS) is an independent set with the largest possible number of nodes. Applications of MIS include scheduling, resource allocation, and network design.\n"
msgstr "Set tak bersandar ialah subset nod dalam graf supaya tiada dua nod terpilih berkongsi satu tepi. Set tak bersandar maksimum (MIS) ialah set tak bersandar dengan bilangan nod terbesar yang mungkin. Aplikasi MIS termasuk penjadualan, peruntukan sumber, dan reka bentuk rangkaian.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "MIS is NP-hard. In an exhaustive search, every additional node doubles the number of subsets to consider, so this approach is impractical even for moderately sized graphs. QOBLIB includes MIS as one of its ten problem classes, so it is a useful benchmark for evaluating quantum optimization workflows on real hardware.\n"
msgstr "MIS ialah NP-hard. Dalam carian lengkap, setiap nod tambahan menggandakan bilangan subset yang perlu dipertimbangkan, jadi pendekatan ini tidak praktikal walaupun untuk graf bersaiz sederhana. QOBLIB memasukkan MIS sebagai salah satu daripada sepuluh kelas masalahnya, jadi ia ialah penanda aras yang berguna untuk menilai aliran kerja pengoptimuman kuantum pada perkakasan sebenar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mathematical formulation {#mathematical-formulation}"
msgstr "Perumusan matematik {#mathematical-formulation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Given an undirected graph $G = (V, E)$, assign a binary variable $x_v$ to each node $v$:\n"
msgstr "Diberi graf tak berarah $G = (V, E)$, tetapkan pemboleh ubah binari $x_v$ kepada setiap nod $v$:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$x_v = 1$ if node $v$ is selected.\n"
msgstr "$x_v = 1$ jika nod $v$ dipilih.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$x_v = 0$ otherwise.\n"
msgstr "$x_v = 0$ otherwise.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [binary linear formulation](https://github.com/ZIB-AOPT/QOBLIB/tree/main/07-independentset/models/binary_linear) maximizes the number of selected nodes while preventing both endpoints of any edge from being selected:\n"
msgstr "[Perumusan linear binari](https://github.com/ZIB-AOPT/QOBLIB/tree/main/07-independentset/models/binary_linear) memaksimumkan bilangan nod terpilih sambil menghalang kedua-dua hujung mana-mana tepi daripada dipilih:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\max_{x} \\quad & \\sum_{v \\in V} x_v \\\\\n"
"\\text{subject to} \\quad & x_v + x_w \\leq 1 && \\forall (v,w) \\in E, \\\\\n"
"& x_v \\in \\{0,1\\} && \\forall v \\in V.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\max_{x} \\quad & \\sum_{v \\in V} x_v \\\\\n"
"\\text{subject to} \\quad & x_v + x_w \\leq 1 && \\forall (v,w) \\in E, \\\\\n"
"& x_v \\in \\{0,1\\} && \\forall v \\in V.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The objective counts the selected nodes. Together, the edge constraints ensure that the selected nodes form an independent set.\n"
msgstr "Objektif mengira nod terpilih. Bersama-sama, kekangan tepi memastikan nod terpilih membentuk set tak bersandar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial uses QOBLIB's [binary unconstrained formulation](https://github.com/ZIB-AOPT/QOBLIB/tree/main/07-independentset/models/binary_unconstrained), which replaces the edge constraints with quadratic penalties:\n"
msgstr "Tutorial ini menggunakan [perumusan binari tanpa kekangan](https://github.com/ZIB-AOPT/QOBLIB/tree/main/07-independentset/models/binary_unconstrained) QOBLIB, yang menggantikan kekangan tepi dengan penalti kuadratik:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\max_{x \\in \\{0,1\\}^{|V|}} \\quad \\sum_{v \\in V} x_v - 2 \\sum_{(v,w) \\in E} x_v x_w.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\max_{x \\in \\{0,1\\}^{|V|}} \\quad \\sum_{v \\in V} x_v - 2 \\sum_{(v,w) \\in E} x_v x_w.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Whenever both endpoints of an edge are selected, the second term subtracts two from the objective. This penalty makes a conflicting selection less favorable than keeping either endpoint alone. The resulting objective is a QUBO, which is the input format that SQOA Solver accepts.\n"
msgstr "Apabila kedua-dua hujung tepi dipilih, sebutan kedua menolak dua daripada objektif. Penalti ini menjadikan pilihan yang bercanggah kurang menguntungkan berbanding mengekalkan salah satu hujung sahaja. Objektif yang terhasil ialah QUBO, iaitu format input yang diterima oleh SQOA Solver.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why use SQOA Solver? {#why-use-sqoa-solver}"
msgstr "Mengapa menggunakan SQOA Solver? {#why-use-sqoa-solver}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Many quantum optimization approaches assign one qubit to each binary variable, so the capacity of the quantum hardware can directly limit the problem size. SQOA Solver combines several reduction and hybrid-computing techniques to ease this restriction:\n"
msgstr "Banyak pendekatan pengoptimuman kuantum menetapkan satu qubit kepada setiap pemboleh ubah binari, jadi kapasiti perkakasan kuantum boleh terus mengehadkan saiz masalah. SQOA Solver menggabungkan beberapa teknik pengurangan dan pengkomputeran hibrid untuk melonggarkan sekatan ini:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**It can tackle problems with more binary variables than the QPU has qubits.** Presolve applies reduction rules that can fix variables and simplify the remaining QUBO while preserving at least one optimal solution. Empirically, presolve can also make the remaining QUBO sparser, which helps the QRAC-based encoding that follows it.\n"
msgstr "**Ia boleh menangani masalah dengan lebih banyak pemboleh ubah binari daripada bilangan qubit pada QPU.** Presolve menerapkan peraturan pengurangan yang boleh menetapkan pemboleh ubah dan memudahkan QUBO yang tinggal sambil mengekalkan sekurang-kurangnya satu penyelesaian optimum. Secara empirik, presolve juga boleh menjadikan QUBO yang tinggal lebih jarang, yang membantu pengekodan berasaskan QRAC yang mengikutinya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  The solver then uses a QRAC-based encoding derived from Quantum Random Access Optimization (QRAO) [\\[3\\]](#references) to represent multiple variables (up to three) with no direct QUBO interaction on the same qubit.\n"
msgstr "  Penyelesai kemudian menggunakan pengekodan berasaskan QRAC yang diterbitkan daripada Quantum Random Access Optimization (QRAO) [\\[3\\]](#references) untuk mewakili berbilang pemboleh ubah (sehingga tiga) tanpa interaksi QUBO langsung pada qubit yang sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  The reductions from presolve and encoding depend on the problem structure. For example, in this tutorial, a 200-variable problem uses only 67 qubits.\n"
"* **It can be less sensitive to hardware noise.** Sample-based quantum diagonalization [\\[4\\]](#references), [\\[5\\]](#references) uses the QPU to sample bitstrings but performs the diagonalization classically. This avoids repeated QPU evaluations for variational parameter updates and can reduce the impact of noise on the optimization workflow.\n"
"* **It automates the workflow from presolve through post-processing.** You provide a correctly formatted QUBO instance and select a backend. SQOA Solver then runs the whole workflow automatically. It applies presolve, maps the classical variables to a relaxed quantum problem, constructs and transpiles the sampling circuits, performs quantum sampling and classical diagonalization, rounds and refines the assignment, and reconstructs and evaluates the classical solution.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Pengurangan daripada presolve dan pengekodan bergantung pada struktur masalah. Contohnya, dalam tutorial ini, masalah 200 pemboleh ubah hanya menggunakan 67 qubit.\n"
"* **Ia boleh kurang sensitif terhadap hingar perkakasan.** Pepenyetriaan pepenjuru kuantum berasaskan sampel [\\[4\\]](#references), [\\[5\\]](#references) menggunakan QPU untuk mensampel rentetan bit tetapi melakukan pepenjuruan secara klasik. Ini mengelakkan penilaian QPU berulang untuk kemas kini parameter variasi dan boleh mengurangkan kesan hingar pada aliran kerja pengoptimuman.\n"
"* **Ia mengautomasikan aliran kerja daripada presolve hingga pascapemprosesan.** Anda menyediakan instans QUBO yang diformat dengan betul dan memilih Backend. SQOA Solver kemudian menjalankan keseluruhan aliran kerja secara automatik. Ia menerapkan presolve, memetakan pemboleh ubah klasik kepada masalah kuantum yang dilonggarkan, membina dan mentranspil litar pensampelan, melakukan pensampelan kuantum dan pepenjuruan klasik, membundarkan dan memperhalus penetapan, serta membina semula dan menilai penyelesaian klasik.\n"

